es_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/deployments","created_at":"2014-06-12T16:00:38Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T22:36:14Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-12T23:00:16Z","git_url":"git://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:bazelbuild/bazel.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel","homepage":"https://bazel.build","size":992874,"stargazers_count":24886,"watchers_count":24886,"language":"Java","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":4359,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1819,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["bazel","build","build-system","correct","fast","multi-language","scalable","test"],"visibility":"public","forks":4359,"open_issues":1819,"watchers":24886,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Description of the problem:\r\n\r\nWhen using `genrule` on macOS, the output file always has permissions `-r-xr-xr-x`, even if `executable = 0` is specified.\r\n\r\n### Minimal example to reproduce the problem:\r\n\r\n`BUILD.bazel`:\r\n```python\r\ngenrule(\r\n    name = \"gen-foo\",\r\n    outs = [\"foo\"],\r\n    cmd = \"echo > $@\",\r\n    executable = 0,\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nExample run:\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ bazel build :gen-foo\r\n...\r\n$ ls -l bazel-genfiles/foo\r\n-r-xr-xr-x  1 user  group  1 Jul 11 16:10 bazel-genfiles/foo\r\n```\r\n\r\n`foo` has executable permissions, but it should not.\r\n\r\nNote that the [documentation for the `genrule` `executable` attribute](https://docs.bazel.build/versions/master/be/general.html#genrule.executable) states that default value for `executable` is `0`. So, by default, it seems that all `genrule`s are generating files with executable permissions.\r\n\r\n### Environment info\r\n* Operating System: macOS Sierra 10.12.5\r\n* Bazel version: `release 0.5.2-homebrew`\r\n\r\nNothing relevant by searching the web. Checked StackOverflow and `bazel-discuss` with the search term \"bazel genrule executable\".\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/918 is possibly relevant.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/3359/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/3359/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]